  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA SRHR 2013-14</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNFPA SRHR 2013-14</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;det till UNFPA, som &#xe4;r ett komplement till UNFPAs k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d, syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra indikatorerna inom h&#xe4;lsosektorn g&#xe4;llande m&#xf6;dra-och barnh&#xe4;lsov&#xe5;rd, f&#xf6;rebyggande av HIV och allm&#xe4;nna insatser f&#xf6;r att      minska fattigdomen som ett resultat av oh&#xe4;lsa. St&#xf6;det &#xe4;r i linje med  m&#xe5;len f&#xf6;r h&#xe4;lsosektorn: f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad tillg&#xe5;ng till h&#xe4;lso- och sjukv&#xe5;rd  f&#xf6;r fattiga m&#xe4;nniskor och minskad spridning av HIV/AIDS.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The support to UNFPA, which is complimentary to UNFPA core support,   aims to contribute to improving the health sector indicators under    maternal and child health, HIV prevention as well general             interventions to alleviate poverty as a results of ill health. Sweden has supported UNFPA core and project support since 2011. The support  in line with the health sector objective.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Update as of 24 April 2015:The overall goal of the project is to improve the status of sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR) of the people of UgandaObjectives: within 24 months time from project start:1) To increase coverage for selected sexual and reproductive health services in the 8 UNFPA/GOU country program focus districts and 5 HIV thematic districts2) To strengthen capacity of leadership of 9 cultural and 3 religious institutions for their (re)engagement in HIV prevention and promotion of FP/MH and GBV services</narrative>
  </description>
